# Git conventions

- Commit only when the user asks.
- Prefer small commits that match one tracer-bullet slice.
- Message style: imperative, why-focused (e.g. `docs: bootstrap agent OS for Admin web`).
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, keys, tokens).
- Do not force-push `main` unless the user explicitly requests it.
